    "t": "Thank you."
  },
  {
    "s": 2749.8,
    "e": 2750.6,
    "t": "Thank you."
  },
  {
    "s": 2760.0,
    "e": 2761.6,
    "t": "Thank you, my dear."
  },
  {
    "s": 2968.9,
    "e": 2971.2,
    "t": "[Unclear dialogue addressed to Djaffar]"
  },
  {
    "s": 3448.0,
    "e": 3451.0,
    "t": "But Algerians weren't fighting\nthe French."
  },
  {
    "s": 3451.3,
    "e": 3454.6,
    "t": "They were fighting colonialism!"
  },
  {
    "s": 3459.9,
    "e": 3462.2,
    "t": "And if colonialism\nstood no chance,"
  },
  {
    "s": 3462.6,
    "e": 3464.8,
    "t": "it wasn't because\nwe were better armed."
  },
  {
    "s": 3472.9,
    "e": 3474.9,
    "t": "Yes, to die for this land!"
  },
  {
    "s": 3478.7,
    "e": 3482.6,
    "t": "Their soldiers arrived by boat\nand left in coffins,"
  },
  {
    "s": 3482.7,
    "e": 3484.4,
    "t": "with just one phrase on their lips."
  },
  {
    "s": 3487.2,
    "e": 3489.1,
    "t": "But today, my brothers,"
  },
  {
    "s": 3489.2,
    "e": 3492.8,
    "t": "who dares treat an Algerian\nlike a nobody?"
  },
  {
    "s": 3492.9,
    "e": 3494.0,
    "t": "No one!"
  },
  {
    "s": 3494.9,
    "e": 3496.8,
    "t": "Who dares forbid an Algerian"
  },
  {
    "s": 3497.2,
    "e": 3499.6,
    "t": "to cross the land of his forefathers?"
  },
  {
    "s": 3499.7,
    "e": 3500.9,
    "t": "No one!"
  },
  {
    "s": 3501.0,
    "e": 3505.0,
    "t": "Who dares forbid an Algerian\nto travel from Australia to America?"
  },
  {
    "s": 3505.1,
    "e": 3506.2,
    "t": "No one!"
  },
  {
    "s": 3507.0,
    "e": 3508.3,
    "t": "Who can even"
  },
  {
    "s": 3509.0,
